        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/965338?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Currently, Firefox/Android shows resizable control with the <code class=\"notranslate\">resize</code> property, but it doesn't work well due to bug 1618678 and bug 1776834.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">So this PR updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">resize</code> property support in Firefox/Android.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27287",
            "title": "Update CSS resize support for Firefox/Android",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-14T05:21:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-14T05:20:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "makotokato",
                "url": "https://github.com/makotokato"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Microsoft Edge for the <code class=\"notranslate\">set</code> SVG element. Considering the support data for all other browsers, it seems unlikely that Edge support came any later.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27285",
            "title": "Update Edge data for set SVG element",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-13T17:48:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-13T17:47:50.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Microsoft Edge for the <code class=\"notranslate\">foreignObject</code> SVG element. Considering the support data for all other browsers, it seems unlikely that Edge support came any later.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27283",
            "title": "Update Edge data for foreignObject SVG element",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-13T00:54:05.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-07-13T00:53:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for all browsers for the <code class=\"notranslate\">text-orientation</code> CSS property. The data comes from manual testing, running test code through BrowserStack, SauceLabs, custom VMs and/or locally.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Test Code:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">\n(Using bcd.testCSSProperty() from the collector)\n\n</code></pre></div>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27189",
            "title": "Update all browsers data for text-orientation CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-11T16:54:23.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T05:02:18.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR updates and corrects version values for Chromium (Chrome, Opera, Samsung Internet, WebView Android) for the <code class=\"notranslate\">speak</code> CSS property. The data comes from the <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">mdn-bcd-collector</a> project (v10.13.3).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>Check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openwebdocs/mdn-bcd-collector#reviewing-bcd-changes\">collector's guide on how to review this PR</a>.</em></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tests Used: <a href=\"https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://mdn-bcd-collector.gooborg.com/tests/css/properties/speak</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27188",
            "title": "Chrome 8 added `speak` CSS property",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-11T16:54:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T04:36:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5179191?u=8dd92441fba3cb438759ee98862670ba56f2c67d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR changes all of the statements for Edge ≤79 to mirror from Chrome.  Based upon commit history and the data, it seems that most likely this data was all mirrored from Chrome via the original mirroring script anyways.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27177",
            "title": "Edge ≤79 -> mirror",
            "date_modified": "2025-07-11T16:53:50.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-30T00:59:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "queengooborg",
                "url": "https://github.com/queengooborg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Based on <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">abort</code> event on <code class=\"notranslate\">IDBDatabase</code>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The data was originally removed in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1140067250\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15006\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/15006\">#15006</a>.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #15345.\">Fixes</span>: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1166786936\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/15345\">#15345</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27167",
            "title": "Re-add IDBDatabase abort event",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-30T07:49:57.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-27T14:00:35.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 136 adds support to the MediaRecorder API for HEVC encoding, introducing the hvc1.* codec string, and adds new codecs (hev1.* and avc3.*) supporting variable resolution video in MP4. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6375884229181440</a> for more details.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for this support to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder()</code> constructor, and to the <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.isTypeSupported()</code> static method.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">MediaRecorder.mimeType</code> property is also related, but it only returns a previously-set value rather than setting a MIME type, so I decided to not add a data point there.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27142",
            "title": "Add data points for Chrome 136 MediaRecorder H26x codec support",
            "date_modified": "2025-06-30T08:45:52.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-06-25T14:32:03.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18311389?u=9ca7c2bf96b915fc275cfcb658fc3fb9ee2f1e0c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Change-set updates chromium support notes for <code class=\"notranslate\">chrome_settings_overrides</code> given that it only has implementations for Windows and MacOS. Version numbers have also been updated to represent more precisely when these features where added.<br>\nNext to this chromium requirements for <code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider</code> properties have also been added as notes to the following properties;</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.favicon_url</code>: Required and needs a HTTP or HTTPS URL which differs from Mozilla's implementation</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.is_default</code>: Given it's a required property within chromium</li>\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.encoding</code>: Required in chromium when <code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider.prepopulated_id</code> is not provided.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sources:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/manifest/chrome-settings-override\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/docs/extensions/reference/manifest/chrome-settings-override</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40717644#comment7\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40717644#comment7</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blob/v35/chrome/common/extensions/docs/templates/articles/settings_override.html#L17-L39\">https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blob/v35/chrome/common/extensions/docs/templates/articles/settings_override.html#L17-L39</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/fe4521c72ade5144b6fb08dcc40afcaf62c67ec3/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/chromium/chromium/commit/fe4521c72ade5144b6fb08dcc40afcaf62c67ec3\">chromium/chromium@<tt>fe4521c</tt></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blame/v58/chrome/common/extensions/api/manifest_types.json#L93-L97\">https://github.com/caugner/chromium-releases/blame/v58/chrome/common/extensions/api/manifest_types.json#L93-L97</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also see linked issue below.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #27046.\">closes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3141541483\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27046\">#27046</a></p>\n",
